  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 306 AM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nAs the upper-level ridge continues to flatten through the week, the \nsurface high over our area will gradually move to the southeast. \nThis will allow for upper-level clouds to continue over the region, \nbut will also cause winds to shift more southwesterly. The \nsouthwesterly winds will bring an increase of low-level warm air \nadvection to the area, bringing warmer temperatures for the end of \nthe work week with highs in the low-80s. Ensemble guidance is very \nconfident on this warm up with IQRs of less than 5 degrees.\n\nGuidance shows signs of a pattern change coming this weekend. An \nupper-level shortwave will move through the Mid-Mississippi Valley \nthat will bring cooler temperatures and a chance for widespread \nrainfall. Both the LREF and NBM guidance shows a slight cool down \nstarting on Saturday and going into next week, with high \ntemperatures in the upper-60s and low-70s each day. Each day's \nentire IQR for the weekend and beyond are below the 25th percentiles \nof Friday's high temperatures giving more precedent of a cool down. \nThis system will bring a return of moisture into the area, which \nshould result in widespread rain showers Saturday afternoon/night. \nEnsemble guidance shows a 70-90% chance of measurable rainfall \n(greater than 0.01 inches) by Sunday morning, with a 40-50% chance \nof seeing 0.25 inches or greater by the same time. Early next week \nensemble guidance shows there could be another shortwave move \nthrough the area that could bring widespread beneficial\nrainfall.",
